.TH geectl-request-file-add-role 1  "geectl-request-file-add-role 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-file\-add\-role \- File an add\-role request: grant a person or a group a role on a project or a package
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request file\-add\-role\fR [\fB\-\-target\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-person\fR] [\fB\-\-person\-role\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR] [\fB\-\-group\-role\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-target\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-description\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
File an add\-role request: grant a person or a group a role on a project or a package
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The project the role is granted on
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-package\fR \fI<TARGET_PACKAGE>\fR
The package the role is granted on; omit for a project\-level grant
.TP
\fB\-\-person\fR \fI<PERSON>\fR
The person granted the role
.TP
\fB\-\-person\-role\fR \fI<PERSON_ROLE>\fR
The role granted to the person
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
The group granted the role
.TP
\fB\-\-group\-role\fR \fI<GROUP_ROLE>\fR
The role granted to the group
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
The request description. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a description may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
